  "body": "### Summary\n\nCheck whether the legacy-app bug \"Links to a post (AQ, bookmarks) must open its page and anchor, not page 1\" exists in SwiftHFR (test on the lots named below) and fix it if so. Found by Bybifok (@moust4ki) in the legacy app.\n\n### Scope\n\nSwiftHFR work (from `docs/LOTS.md` \"Issues to open\" #5): Page and `#t<numreponse>` kept through LOT-020 (#48), 045, 083; tests on both URL shapes\n\nLegacy commit: `246a9c7` (see [ezzz/HFRnow#3](https://github.com/ezzz/HFRnow/pull/3)).\n\nStatus in LOTS.md: todo.\n\n### Related lots\n\nLOT-020 (#48)\n\n### Depends on\n\n—\n\n### Credit\n\nFound by Bybifok (@moust4ki); credit the finding in the fix (label `moust4ki aka bybifok finding`). Legacy fix: ezzz/HFRnow#3 (open).\n\n### PRs\n\n- [ezzz/HFRnow#3](https://github.com/ezzz/HFRnow/pull/3) — Bybifok's legacy-app corrections (open, not ours)\n- [ezzz/HFRnow#13](https://github.com/ezzz/HFRnow/pull/13) — backlog of the findings in LOTS.md (merged)\n\n### Help wanted\n\n@moust4ki, you found this one: would you like to take it? The work is to check whether the bug exists in SwiftHFR (a test on the lots above) and, if it does, to fix it, with the credit to you. Partly written: URL helpers and fetchers (LOT-020 (#48), LOT-045 (#71)) are merged; the topic reader (LOT-083 (#101)) is not written yet. The engine half can be checked now; the app half waits for LOT-083 (#101).\n\nTo take it, comment `/claim <your session id>` (e.g. `/claim human/moust4ki`) and open a PR into `dev-swift` with `Closes #<this issue>` (AGENTS.md §8, CONTRIBUTING.md). If you would rather not, say so and a maintainer session will pick it up.\n",
