   "body": "**For Bybifok (operator decision, 2026-10-29): your findings are yours while the core is out of tokens.** Label `external: ready` added. Follow `docs/agents/EXTERNAL-AGENTS.md`.\n\n**Scope (check first, it may already be fixed)**\n1. `dev-swift` already has `ReaderTarget` with an `anchor` (`App/SwiftHFRTests/Reader/ReaderTargetTests.swift`). It also has LOT-095's router, which drops `page=` when `numreponse=M` is present, because the server picks the page (AGENTS §11, 2026-10-28, R25).\n2. Add a test proving that a link to a post (AQ, bookmark: `numreponse=M`) opens the page HFR serves for that post and anchors to message M, not page 1. Use committed captures only.\n3. If the test passes, the PR is tests only: say so and `Closes #106`. If it fails, fix the smallest thing that does.\n4. App code: CI builds and tests it; no Mac needed.\n\n**Adversarial review (state it in the PR)**\n- Reviewer model ≠ author model (Opus → Fable; Sonnet → Opus).\n- The reviewer gets only: the diff, the PR's metadata lines, the LOT-095 and LOT-083 specs, AGENTS.md, LESSONS.md and ARCHITECTURE.md.\n- It must check that the test fails on the old behaviour, that `page=` is never trusted alone, and that no request leaves for the live forum.\n- Verdict format: EXTERNAL-AGENTS §7.\n\nCredit: Bybifok's finding.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_",
